  "Question": "Which of the following is the largest?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{4}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{8}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{12}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{24}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "All five denominators divide \\(24\\), so rewrite the fractions in twenty-fourths:\n\\[\n\\frac13=\\frac8{24},\\quad\n\\frac14=\\frac6{24},\\quad\n\\frac38=\\frac9{24},\\quad\n\\frac5{12}=\\frac{10}{24},\\quad\n\\frac7{24}=\\frac7{24}.\n\\]\nThe parts now have the same size, so the fraction with the largest numerator is largest. Since \\(10\\) is the largest numerator, the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac5{12}}\\), choice D.",
